# Source-derived semantics

- The source contains one instruction paragraph followed by one empty div with a 200px by 200px content box.
- The tested declaration is background: repeat-x bottom url("support/blue15x15.png") green; and is preserved verbatim.
- The green field and horizontally repeated blue image at the bottom make image, repeat, position, color, and token ordering visually observable.

# Compatibility adjustments

- Visible text uses text and the test box uses a class-scoped view.
- Content-box sizing and explicit body/paragraph spacing reproduce Web setup without relying on margin collapse.
- The card-local blue15x15.png is copied byte-for-byte from the reference-clean source cache.

# Current Lynx API-doc basis

- Lynx documents background, URL images, named colors, repeat-x, and position, but this exact combination remains pending visual verification.
